.TH FTA 1 "" "fta 1.0.0" "File Transfer for All"
.SH NAME
fta \- transfer files over SFTP, FTP, SMB, WebDAV, S3, HTTP, clouds and to nearby devices
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B fta
[\-h] [\-\-limit LIMIT] {cp,sync,serve,send,receive,cloud,encrypt,decrypt,keygen,share,stats,ёж,hedgehog,ipfs,tailscale,peers,history,ls,stat,mkdir,rm,schemes} ...
.SH DESCRIPTION
fta is the command line of File Transfer for All. Locations are local paths, URLs such as sftp://user@host/dir, smb://server/share, ftp://, dav://, s3://bucket, rclone://cloud/ and @connection:/path for connections saved in the app.
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
show this help message and exit
.TP
.B \-\-limit
speed limit for all transfers, e.g. 500K or 2M (bytes per second)
.SH COMMANDS
.SS cp
copy a file or, with \-r, a directory
.PP
.B fta cp [\-h] [\-r] [\-\-resume] [\-\-verify] [\-\-retries N] [\-\-src\-opt KEY=VALUE] [\-\-dst\-opt KEY=VALUE] source destination
.TP
.B source
file or folder: a path, a URL or @connection:/path
.TP
.B destination
where to put it; a folder or a path ending in / receives it by name
.TP
.B \-r, \-\-recursive
copy directories recursively
.TP
.B \-\-resume
continue partial files instead of resending them
.TP
.B \-\-verify
compare SHA\-256 of both sides after each file
.TP
.B \-\-retries
retry N times, resuming each time
.TP
.B \-\-src\-opt
option for the source transport (repeatable)
.TP
.B \-\-dst\-opt
option for the destination transport (repeatable)
.SS sync
mirror a folder; changed files send only their changed blocks
.PP
.B fta sync [\-h] [\-\-delete] [\-\-src\-opt KEY=VALUE] [\-\-dst\-opt KEY=VALUE] source destination
.TP
.B source
the folder to mirror
.TP
.B destination
the folder that becomes its copy
.TP
.B \-\-delete
also delete destination files missing from the source
.TP
.B \-\-src\-opt
option for the source transport (repeatable)
.TP
.B \-\-dst\-opt
option for the destination transport (repeatable)
.SS serve
run the SSH/SFTP server for PuTTY, WinSCP, psftp, ssh
.PP
.B fta serve [\-h] [\-\-root ROOT] [\-\-port PORT] [\-\-host HOST] [\-\-user USER] [\-\-set\-password]
.TP
.B \-\-root
shared folder (default: from settings, else ~/FTA Shared)
.TP
.B \-\-port
port (default: from settings, 2222)
.TP
.B \-\-host
address to listen on (default: all)
.TP
.B \-\-user
login name (default: from settings, fta)
.TP
.B \-\-set\-password
ask for a new password and save its hash
.SS send
send files or folders to a nearby device
.PP
.B fta send [\-h] [\-\-pin PIN] [\-\-wait WAIT] target PATH [PATH ...]
.TP
.B target
device name (see `fta peers`), fta:// link from its QR code, or host[:port]
.TP
.B PATH

.TP
.B \-\-pin
PIN shown on the receiving device, if it asks for one
.TP
.B \-\-wait
seconds to look for the device by name (default 5)
.SS receive
accept files from nearby devices
.PP
.B fta receive [\-h] [\-\-dir DIR] [\-\-port PORT] [\-\-pin PIN] [\-y] [\-\-qr]
.TP
.B \-\-dir
where to save (default: from settings, else Downloads/FTA)
.TP
.B \-\-port
port (default 53318; 0 picks a free one)
.TP
.B \-\-pin
require this PIN from senders
.TP
.B \-y, \-\-yes
accept every offer without asking
.TP
.B \-\-qr
print a QR code with this device\(aqs link
.SS cloud
cloud drives via rclone: list, add, remove, install
.PP
.B fta cloud [\-h] {list,add,remove,install} [name] [type] [KEY=VALUE ...]
.TP
.B action

.TP
.B name
name for the cloud, used as rclone://NAME/
.TP
.B type
drive, dropbox, yandex, onedrive, mailru, webdav, …
.TP
.B KEY=VALUE
e.g. user=me pass=secret
.SS encrypt
encrypt files to FILE.age (age format; asks for a passphrase)
.PP
.B fta encrypt [\-h] [\-r RECIPIENT] FILE [FILE ...]
.TP
.B FILE

.TP
.B \-r, \-\-recipient
age1… public key instead of a passphrase
.SS decrypt
decrypt FILE.age (with this device\(aqs key or a passphrase)
.PP
.B fta decrypt [\-h] [\-i IDENTITY] FILE [FILE ...]
.TP
.B FILE

.TP
.B \-i, \-\-identity
file with an AGE\-SECRET\-KEY\-1…
.SS keygen
show this device\(aqs age public key, for others to encrypt to
.PP
.B fta keygen [\-h]
.SS share
give a file or folder away by a one\-time link and QR code
.PP
.B fta share [\-h] [\-\-ttl TTL] [\-\-many] [\-\-port PORT] path
.TP
.B path
file or folder (sent as a zip)
.TP
.B \-\-ttl
how long the link works: 10m, 1h, 1d (default 1h)
.TP
.B \-\-many
allow more than one download until it expires
.TP
.B \-\-port
port (default: any free one)
.SS stats
totals from the journal; \-\-card writes a shareable SVG
.PP
.B fta stats [\-h] [\-\-days DAYS] [\-\-card FILE.svg]
.TP
.B \-\-days
only the last N days
.TP
.B \-\-card
write a summary card picture
.SS ёж
a hedgehog
.PP
.B fta ёж [\-h]
.SS ipfs
publish files to IPFS through the local node (read with fta cp ipfs://CID)
.PP
.B fta ipfs [\-h] [\-\-api API] {add} FILE [FILE ...]
.TP
.B action

.TP
.B FILE

.TP
.B \-\-api
the node\(aqs API (default http://127.0.0.1:5001)
.SS tailscale
devices in your tailnet; with a device and files, send to it
.PP
.B fta tailscale [\-h] [\-\-pin PIN] [target] [PATH ...]
.TP
.B target
device name or 100.x address
.TP
.B PATH

.TP
.B \-\-pin
PIN, if the receiving app asks for one
.SS peers
list FTA devices on the local network
.PP
.B fta peers [\-h] [\-\-wait WAIT]
.TP
.B \-\-wait
seconds to listen (default 3)
.SS history
show the transfer journal
.PP
.B fta history [\-h] [\-n N] [\-\-csv FILE]
.TP
.B \-n
how many entries (default 20)
.TP
.B \-\-csv
export the whole journal to a CSV file
.SS ls
list a directory
.PP
.B fta ls [\-h] [\-\-opt KEY=VALUE] location
.TP
.B location
a path, a URL or @connection:/path
.TP
.B \-\-opt
transport option (repeatable)
.SS stat
show one file or directory
.PP
.B fta stat [\-h] [\-\-opt KEY=VALUE] location
.TP
.B location
a path, a URL or @connection:/path
.TP
.B \-\-opt
transport option (repeatable)
.SS mkdir
create a directory
.PP
.B fta mkdir [\-h] [\-\-opt KEY=VALUE] [\-p] location
.TP
.B location
a path, a URL or @connection:/path
.TP
.B \-\-opt
transport option (repeatable)
.TP
.B \-p, \-\-parents
no error if it exists
.SS rm
delete a file or an empty directory
.PP
.B fta rm [\-h] [\-\-opt KEY=VALUE] location
.TP
.B location
a path, a URL or @connection:/path
.TP
.B \-\-opt
transport option (repeatable)
.SS schemes
list supported URL schemes
.PP
.B fta schemes [\-h]
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/fta/config.toml
settings and saved connections (FTA_CONFIG, FTA_DATA_DIR change it; an fta\-data folder next to the program makes it portable)
.TP
.I ~/.config/fta/journal.jsonl
the transfer journal (fta history, fta stats)
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B FTA_<SETTING>
any setting, e.g. FTA_RETRIES=5 or FTA_SPEED_LIMIT_KIB=2048
.TP
.B FTA_RCLONE
the rclone program to use for clouds
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
fta cp \-\-resume \-\-verify https://example.com/big.iso ./
fta sync ./photos sftp://me@nas.local/backup/photos \-\-delete
fta send "Laptop" ./report.pdf
fta share ./photos \-\-ttl 1d
fta encrypt \-r age1... secret.pdf
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
Project page: https://github.com/Zaxar1231/File\-transfer\-for\-all
